.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class USER>
.br
class csmp::H2O_CO2_NaCl_FlowFunctions< dim, USER >"\fBH2O_CO2_NaCl_FlowFunctions\fP: Saturation functions and fluid properties combined into flow functions for the H2O + CO2+ NaCl system\&. 

Use in conjunction with the \fBPhaseStateFinder_H2O_CO2_NaCl\fP for compositional simulation in a mass-based transport framework\&. Plugs into a suitable FlowFunctionsModule within the Colleoli class framework for a multiphase-multicomponent transport scheme\&.

.PP
Generate all relevant input values for transport scheme from SaturationFunctions and \fBFluid\fP modules, using the constitutive relationships specified therein\&. Gets the fluid properties by interpolation from the \fBElement\fP nodes to its barycentre\&.

.PP
Expects that the water saturation, the fluid densities and viscosities to be placed on the element nodes, while all material (k, phi, bcp etc\&.), and rocktype related parameters are placed on the element\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
all parameters are weighted by the element thickness which is 1 for iso-dimensional elements\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
Stephan Matthai 
.RE
.PP
\fBDate\fP
.RS 4
7/1/2019
.RE
.PP
@discussion Phase state cannot be interpolated between nodes ! If we read the system state from the element, in the case of an element-based phase state calculation, it may be entirely different from that computed at the nodes and therefore, we may try to fetch densities and viscosities which do not exist ?! 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class USER> double \fBcsmp::H2O_CO2_NaCl_FlowFunctions\fP< dim, USER >::AdvectionMultiplier (\fBElement\fP< dim > * const e) const"

.PP
multiplier for advection viscosity coefficient in the case of non-linear advection fractional flow derivative for wetting phase = 0\&.

.PP
If not overloaded, this returns the derivative of the fractional flow function at the current saturation of the wetting phase (see Helmig, 1997, p\&. 108, eqn\&. 3\&.74, term 2 (first part)\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class USER> double \fBcsmp::H2O_CO2_NaCl_FlowFunctions\fP< dim, USER >::CapillaryDiffusionMultiplier (\fBElement\fP< dim > * const e) const"

.PP
mass diffusion coefficient for the non-linear diffusion of saturation due to the saturation dependent dpc/ds When capillary spreading is simulated using the FE method, it can be modelled as a nonlinear diffusion process\&. Nonlinear because the driving gradient varies with saturation\&.

.PP
qm_capillary = rhon * k * lambda_overbar * dpc/dsw * grad_sw ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ diffusion multiplier

.PP
See Helmig, 1997, p\&. 108, eqn\&. 3\&.74, term 1\&. This takes into account the permeability in direction of flow x lambda_overbar x pc-gradient\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
lambda overbar contains the fluid densities and viscosities\&. 
.RE
.PP

