.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class USER> double \fBcsmp::H2O_CO2_NaCl_FlowFunctions\fP< dim, USER >::DiffusionMultiplier (\fBElement\fP< dim > * const e, uint32_t phase) const"

.PP
mass diffusion coefficient for CO2 in water saturated porous medium; use phase=1 Returns the diffusivity of CO2 in the porous medium saturated with water, using the diffusivity calculated by the PhaseStateFinder as an input\&. The calculation of the diffusivity of water in CO2 (phase == 0) is not implemented yet\&.

.PP
The scaling of the diffusivity is done with the porosity, not the permeability\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
For phase=1 this coefficient is defined only for aq, aq_carb and aq_carb_salt phase states, else zero is returned\&.
.RE
.PP
@discussion Diffusion caclulations make sense only for a higher order accurate transport scheme because the first-order scheme already is more diffusive than is physically realistic\&. 
